# Official public Telegram TEST ONLY application identifiers for local testing, not distribution.
# Source: https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop/blob/dev/docs/api_credentials.md
# Official guidance: https://core.telegram.org/api/obtaining_api_id#using-telegram-s-open-source-code
# These test credentials have server-side limits. Obtain your own API ID/Hash at
# https://my.telegram.org before publishing an application.
# Identifiers are embedded in the binary and are extractable; they are not account
# passwords and do not authorize access to a Telegram account.
#
# Neither Cargo nor the app automatically loads dotenv files. A plain cargo run -r
# does not read this file. option_env! reads credentials at compile time, so export
# the variables before building/running through Cargo.
# This file is a template only; never source it for builds or packaging.
# Copy it to .env.local if absent and replace the samples with your own values.
# From the repository root, load your private local configuration (bash/zsh):
# (
#   set +x
#   set -a
#   . ./.env.local || exit 1
#   set +a
#   cargo run -r -p teleark-gui --bin teleark --locked
# )
# The subshell leaves the parent shell environment unchanged. Supply the variables
# on every build/run: a later plain cargo run -r uses its current environment and
# may rebuild without embedded defaults. Passing variables only to an already
# built executable does not change its compiled credentials; rebuild through Cargo.
#
# For personal values, copy this file to .env.local only if that file does not
# already exist, set its permissions to 0600, and edit values locally.
# For packaging, run scripts/build-local.sh before scripts/package-macos.sh.
# Preserve existing local configuration.
# Source only trusted files. Never print personal values, enable shell tracing,
# or commit .env.local. The local packaging helper requires both values.
# Personal credentials saved in the app take precedence.
# See docs/DEVELOPMENT.md for more details.
TELEARK_DISTRIBUTION_TELEGRAM_API_ID=17349
TELEARK_DISTRIBUTION_TELEGRAM_API_HASH=344583e45741c457fe1862106095a5eb
